# foundry
out/
cache/
broadcast/

# node
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# os
.DS_Store
foundry.lock

# epoch artifacts produced by the keeper
offchain/data/
front/dist/
test/_Debug.t.sol
public/

# Operational runbooks, and this is a GLOB rather than a list of names: a new
# one is written under a new name every time, and a list only ever matches the
# files that existed the day it was typed.
docs/LAUNCH*
docs/RELAUNCH.md
docs/relaunch-runbook.html
docs/PAYD_RUNBOOK.md
docs/DEPLOY_HOSTS.md
docs/REHEARSAL.md
docs/WEB_READINESS.md

# A runbook does not stop being one because it is executable. Nothing public
# depends on it, and nothing about what the contracts do is verified by reading
# it.
script/fly-secrets.sh

# Transaction bundles staged for the Safe's builder. One-off operational
# artifacts: the operation they describe is on-chain once it is executed, and
# the file is of no use to anybody afterwards.
*-tx.json

# The internal audit and review record. Not withheld because it is embarrassing
# — it is the best engineering in the repository. See docs/README.md for why it
# is not here and what stands in its place.
docs/AUDIT_PLAN.md
docs/AUDIT_PLAN_2.md
docs/AUDIT_EXECUTION.md
docs/AUDIT_EXECUTION_2.md
docs/AUDIT_FIXES.md
docs/AUDIT_FIXES_2.md
docs/AUDIT_FIXES_3.md
docs/AUDIT_PAYD.md
docs/REVIEW_3.md
docs/REVIEW_3_AI.md
docs/REVIEW_3_SEALED.md

# Internal planning and strategy. Not secret, and not product documentation
# either: they carry deliberation and options that were never shipped, and a
# published roadmap reads as a set of commitments made by an identifiable team.
PLAN.md
ROADMAP.md
docs/ROADMAP.md
docs/*_PLAN.md
BRAND.md
ESTIMATIONS.md
LAUNCH_2026-09-12.md

# The assistant's working file. Its ENGINEERING rules live in the repository as
# docs/CONVENTIONS.md; what stays here is the part addressed to a collaborator
# rather than to the code.
CLAUDE.md


# v1 production artifacts. They carry real holder addresses and belong on a
# disk, not in a public repository.
offchain/final-artifact-*.json

# The personal denylist the pre-commit hook reads. Never committed: a tracked
# file listing the names it blocks would publish them.
.githooks/identity.local

# The operational and decision record. None of it is a secret; all of it is a
# targeting package if published together.
OPSEC.md
DECISIONS.md
PREFLIGHT.md

# Local tooling and scratch work. Nothing here is part of the product, and
# nothing here needs to be read to verify what the contracts do.
.private/

# Editor and agent configuration. The publication script ships the tree
# VERBATIM, so anything committed here would ship with it — tooling choices
# included. Nothing in it is part of the product.
.claude/

# Coverage output. The CI job publishes it as an artifact; it does not belong
# in the tree.
lcov.info

# Built by `pnpm --filter front build:ticker` into a source directory, because
# `site/` is hand-written and has no build folder of its own. Generated, not source.
site/ticker.js

# A French design export, kept on disk and out of the public squash (2026-10-01).
/Payd Redesign.pdf
